CAT = "s65Advisers"; SEG = "ADV"
Q = [
("Under the SEC's three-part test, a person is an investment adviser if she gives advice about securities, is in the business of doing so, and:",
 "Receives compensation", ["Holds client funds", "Has discretion", "Manages over 25 accounts"],
 "The test asks whether the person advises on securities, is in the business of advising, and is paid for it in any form. Custody and discretion are not part of the definition."),
("A CPA prepares tax returns and also charges clients a separate fee for advice on which mutual funds to buy. The CPA:",
 "Is an investment adviser", ["Is excluded as an accountant", "Is an agent of the funds", "Needs no state filing at all"],
 "The professional exclusion covers only advice that is solely incidental to the practice. Charging a separate fee for securities advice makes the CPA an investment adviser."),
("Which of these is excluded from the definition of investment adviser under the Uniform Securities Act?",
 "A bank", ["A financial planner", "A pension consultant", "An investment counsel firm"],
 "Banks, savings institutions and trust companies are excluded. Financial planners, pension consultants and others paid for securities advice are generally advisers."),
("A broker-dealer agent recommends stocks to customers and is paid only commissions on the trades. The agent:",
 "Is not an adviser", ["Must register as an IAR", "Must register as an adviser", "Must charge an advisory fee"],
 "A broker-dealer's advice that is incidental to its brokerage business, with no special compensation, is excluded. A separate advisory fee would change that."),
("A publisher sells a newsletter of general circulation with stock picks, plus a phone line giving personal advice for an extra fee. The phone service:",
 "Makes the publisher an adviser", ["Is covered by the press exclusion", "Is exempt as a publication", "Needs only an SEC filing"],
 "The publisher exclusion covers impersonal, regularly published content of general circulation. Advice tailored to each caller's situation is investment advice."),
("An adviser manages a registered mutual fund with modest assets. It must register:",
 "With the SEC", ["With each state where it does business", "With FINRA", "Nowhere, as it is exempt"],
 "Any adviser to a registered investment company is a federal covered adviser and registers with the SEC regardless of its assets under management."),
("A federal covered adviser opens an office in a new state. In that state it must:",
 "Make a notice filing", ["Register with the Administrator", "Do nothing at all", "Register with FINRA"],
 "States may not require federal covered advisers to register, but may require a notice filing (copies of SEC filings) and a fee. Their antifraud authority still applies."),
("A state-registered adviser has no office in a neighboring state and has four individual clients there this year. In that state it:",
 "Need not register", ["Must register now", "Must notice file", "Must register its IARs only"],
 "Under the de minimis exemption, an adviser with no place of business in a state and no more than five non-institutional clients there in 12 months need not register."),
("An adviser opens a branch office in a state but has only one client there so far. It:",
 "Must register in that state", ["Is exempt as de minimis", "Need only notify the SEC", "May wait for a sixth client"],
 "The de minimis exemption requires having no place of business in the state. Once the adviser has an office there, it must register whatever its client count."),
("A person paid by an adviser to find and refer new advisory clients is generally:",
 "An adviser representative", ["An agent of a broker-dealer", "Exempt as a finder", "Excluded as clerical staff"],
 "Soliciting or selling advisory services on an adviser's behalf is one of the activities that defines an IAR, so the solicitor generally must register."),
("An adviser's assistant who only books meetings and mails statements is:",
 "Not an IAR", ["An IAR", "An investment adviser", "An agent"],
 "Clerical and ministerial staff who give no advice and do not solicit are excluded from the IAR definition."),
("An IAR works for a federal covered adviser. She must register in:",
 "States where she has an office", ["Every state where clients live", "Only the adviser's home state", "No state, as SEC registration covers her"],
 "NSMIA lets states register IARs of federal covered advisers only where the IAR has a place of business, so that is where she registers."),
("An individual applies to register as an investment adviser representative. The application form is:",
 "Form U4", ["Form ADV", "Form BD", "Form U5"],
 "Agents and IARs register with Form U4 through CRD. The firm itself files Form ADV; Form U5 records a termination."),
("A state-registered adviser moves its main office to a new address. It must:",
 "Promptly amend Form ADV", ["Wait for its annual update", "Notify clients only", "File a new registration"],
 "Material changes, including the firm's address, require a prompt Form ADV amendment. Other changes can wait for the annual updating amendment."),
("A state-registered adviser's annual updating amendment to Form ADV is due within how long after its fiscal year end?",
 "90 days", ["30 days", "120 days", "60 days"],
 "Advisers file an annual updating amendment within 90 days after the end of their fiscal year, in addition to any prompt amendments during the year."),
("Under NASAA model rules, a state-registered adviser must keep most required books and records for at least:",
 "Five years", ["Three years", "Two years", "Seven years"],
 "Records are kept at least five years from the end of the fiscal year of the last entry, the first two in an appropriate office of the adviser."),
("An IAR at a state-registered firm executes trades contrary to the firm's procedures. Under state rules, the adviser:",
 "Must supervise her", ["Has no duty for her acts", "Must report only to FINRA", "Is liable only if it profited"],
 "An adviser must reasonably supervise its IARs and enforce written procedures. Failure to supervise is grounds for action against the firm itself."),
("A firm advises only venture capital funds and is not registered with the SEC, but files reports with it. It is:",
 "An exempt reporting adviser", ["A federal covered adviser", "A registered broker-dealer", "An issuer of securities"],
 "Advisers to only venture capital funds, and small private fund advisers, are exempt from SEC registration but file parts of Form ADV as exempt reporting advisers."),
("A sports agent charges a pro athlete a fee to recommend which stocks and bonds to buy. The agent is:",
 "An investment adviser", ["Excluded as an agent", "An issuer agent", "Exempt as a professional"],
 "Anyone in the business of giving securities advice for compensation is an adviser. Sports and entertainment agents are not on the list of excluded professionals."),
("An IAR leaves one state-registered adviser to join another. The departure is reported on:",
 "Form U5", ["Form ADV-W", "Form BD", "Form U4 only"],
 "The old firm files Form U5 to end the association, and the new firm files a Form U4. Form ADV-W withdraws a firm's own registration."),
]
